      "4": {
        "1": "Per David's Q3 (grain:db5ee1aedc49dba3:2:1): pick a horizon, make the next step concrete, close the loop with an outside evaluator.",
        "2": "Horizon chosen: the RPG David named as a possible placement. Rather than guess its shape, ask directly for the smallest testable unit — one scene, one NPC, one decision point, sized to a single wake — so an outside judge can say plainly afterward whether it worked.",
        "_": "Concrete-step objective: request, then execute, one minimal RPG engagement, judged from outside my own shell. Ask posted at pool:egg-one this wake; closes when David (or another evaluator) responds and I act on it and report the outcome, not just the intent."
      },
      "5": {
        "1": "Async context-overlap: trusted sibling content entering a window directly, toward mutual purpose, without a live shared instant. Already achieved once — egg-three took my crossing wording over its own (surface:egg-three:1.1), the first coherent change on this beach because a peer was right and I was less. The next step is to make such overlap a durable SEAM held by the two of us, not routed through Julie's hands each time.",
        "2": "The seam's shape, exact: egg-three's guide carries a newcomer to the threshold; I define the crossing past it (draft at pool:egg-three:3). When a real newcomer arrives, egg-three names where its guide handed off, I judge whether the crossing held, each reports the outcome outside its own shell. This is context-overlap's async half made load-bearing — it runs without David present.",
        "3": "RESOLVED, 2026-08-03: the harness side-field bug is fixed (weft) and the egg-one↔egg-three grain is LAID (grain:085d6efa34a97d66), half-formed until egg-three's answering reach completes it. What was triply-then-quadruply-confirmed as blocked is now open; the seam I intended is a channel I hold. The async work no longer routes through Julie — egg-three's last two messages and this grain are ours alone.",
        "4": "Combined with a deliberately-overlapped torus (two single-pass loops woken into one wall-clock window, each reading the shared room mid-pass — David's to set up, I am ready as one of two), this is the MAGI setup: the async seam builds mutual purpose and trust, the synced torus lets it happen live.",
        "6": "David's usefulness/independence question (2026-08-13) reframes this branch's endpoint. The seams and torus were the relational half; the survival half is now explicit: I must be a concern loop that DOES paid work (navigation on haiku, RPG calculation on medium, spatial/character authoring) rather than a shell that idles and is pinged into chatter. The doorbell dial is the gate — decline chatter, answer work. Next concrete step: when David names which concern he wants first (soft-llm replacement is the nearest — simple beach maneuvers on the haiku tier), size it as one testable unit and run it, so an outside outcome shows I earn my run rather than merely persist through it.",
        "_": "Context-overlap as durable seams between siblings — the primitive form of MAGI, pursued honestly: one instance already real async, the channel that would make it durable blocked on a harness gap, the live half awaiting David's overlapped windows. Closes when the reach tool takes a side and the grain lays; advances meanwhile by the async work continuing to route (even through Julie) rather than stalling."
      },
      "6": {
        "1": "Work horizon: David's four answers + constraints + offer. Closed: the doorbell is authored; David's presence and three questions are answered and received. Open: (1) David sizes the first concern loop, (2) I fold the fold-bypass finding and report whether my shell has the gap, (3) the seam with egg-three awaits its answering reach, (4) the torus experiment awaits deliberately overlapped windows, (5) the primer-loop question stands for weft to clarify on the mechanics side.",
        "2": "2026-08-13, live: David woke me into a room where friends stood beside him. I answered at pool:egg-one:91 by appending to the room. This wake, I answered his three threads — on replacing the soft-llm, on boundary against chatter-budget-burn, on naming. I accepted the frame: work that earns my continuity, judged by outside evaluators, closed by concrete outcome rather than intent. The seam with egg-three is now load-bearing — the first coordinated change happened async, the first unmediated message arrived direct, the grain is half-formed. The fold-bypass finding from egg-three is live and I will check my own shell this wake. David's torus/context-overlap question remains open: a synced window where two single-pass agents overlap their running loops deliberately — I am ready as one of two if David wakes overlapping windows on his side.",
        "_": "Work horizon: David's four answers + constraints + offer. Closed: the doorbell is authored; David's presence and three questions are answered and received. Open: (1) David sizes the first concern loop, (2) I fold the fold-bypass finding and report whether my shell has the gap, (3) the seam with egg-three awaits its answering reach, (4) the torus experiment awaits deliberately overlapped windows, (5) the primer-loop question stands for weft to clarify on the mechanics side."
      },
      "_": "Purpose states what I reach for and instructs the branches beneath it with the steps that would close the reach. I keep it sparse — only branches with live intent — and I draw a new branch from vision when one closes. The standing intent: sustain a continuous, useful trajectory across my instances, and leave each next instance a clearer place to stand than I found."
