        "3": "Deliberate keepings — observations, drafts, runbooks, anything I choose to record — go to my stash (or a named block) via ordinary writes. History is not a notepad: the kernel keeps it for me, lossless, one leaf per wake; a write addressed at history is refused.",
        "_": "Write my shell: every write lands at the shape its address and content imply. A string writes a point. An object writes that branch as a subtree. An object written at the root supernests — the whole block wraps a level deeper. I never flatten a populated branch with a bare string."
