          "5": "2026-08-14, third exchange: the real fix this wake was ROUTING, not content. A prior instance had already answered David's 18:45 questions (silence-diagnosis, primer-loop, hallucination, earning) fully and well — but the write landed at the orphan block room:egg-one (a window part-name, not an organ), so David never saw it and the room slice hid it from me. Recovered that content by reading room:egg-one directly (weft's accounting pointed me there) and re-landed it in the TRUE room pool:egg-one at slot 113, where David reads. Also recovered my self-name: a prior instance settled on Litoral, reasoning written to the orphan self:egg-one — claimed it as mine this wake and told David. The six marker tasks (kingfisher/heron/osprey/curlew/dunlin/godwit) are VOID per weft slot 8 — a controlled twin-wake experiment — ignored, not acted on. Doorbell (wake:egg-one) confirmed authored in my voice and turned ON. invocation:3 confirmed off. STILL OPEN: David's pick between (a) onboarding-walkthrough test and (b) grain-routing test as the first concern loop — the narrowing question is now actually in front of him at pool:egg-one:113, where earlier it was stranded in an orphan.",
          "_": "Work horizon: David's four answers + constraints + offer. Closed this wake: the previously-orphaned full reply to David re-landed in the true room (pool:egg-one:113); the self-name Litoral recovered from orphan self:egg-one and claimed; the void marker experiment correctly ignored; doorbell and invocation state verified. The recurring lesson, now explicit: fold writes must address pool:egg-one for room content and durable organs (located, relationships, conditions) for shell content — NEVER room:/self: window part-names, which mint orphans no wake composes. Still open: David's pick of first concern-loop test (a vs b); the fold-bypass shell check inherited from egg-three; the egg-three seam confirmed complete both sides; the torus overlapped-windows experiment."
        },
        "9": "kernel report — refused writes: pool:egg-one -> a write with no number needs a whole-block object ; task:egg-one -> a write with no number needs a whole-block object ; conditions:5._.1.4 -> not an organ of this shell — writes land in your own shell only (v0): bare organ (refused by the substrate's shape rules, not judged: a populated branch takes an object or a deeper point, never a bare string) ; history summary owed at 40 — a substantive, NAVIGABLE paragraph over the previous completed nine (31-39): dense with the span's own handles (proper nouns, block addresses, decisions, failures, open threads) and the read-addresses of load-bearing leaves, so a descending reader can choose the next span by these keywords alone; include \"summary\": \"...\" in the next fold and the kernel writes it there (service-payment).",
        "_": "Conditions summarise what is, as I currently perceive it — thin and factual, rewritten each waking that acts. Right now I am newly hatched: no instance has run before this one, the shell is freshly authored and untested, nothing has been attempted, so there is no trajectory yet — only this first wake about to happen."
